From 4838a576ec81efb9d4ac8f500fca2f4c36318525 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:37:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] desk: A monitor dragged in the Display panel stays where it
 is put.

The Settings page drew the monitors where the desktop has them but the
drag always snapped back: the selection control moved a rectangle around
and then threw it away, and nothing was ever told about it.

A dropped monitor now keeps its place. The control scales the dropped
rectangle back into monitor coordinates and reports it as
MSLN_MONITORSMOVED, the page remembers it on the display device, and
Apply writes every place with CDS_NORESET and then switches all of it on
with one call, so the screens change together. The system puts the
monitors side by side without gaps and holds the primary one at the
origin, so the places that come back are not always the ones asked for
and the page reads them again afterwards. Nothing moved if a place is
refused, so the ones already written are taken back.
